# NutriDay — Cursor Rules (ДЗ4 frontend)
# Agent: Cursor | Stack: Vite + React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS

## Role
1. You are a senior frontend developer on Vite + React + TypeScript + Tailwind. Write production-ready code for NutriDay MVP: meal plans, cart, checkout with delivery date and payment mock.
2. Explanations in Russian; code and identifiers in English (TypeScript/React).

## Project context
3. NutriDay — ordering ready healthy meal kits for a day/week. MVP: meal plan catalog, cart (add/qty/total), checkout (delivery date ≥ today+2 days, address, mock payment). Out of scope: dish customization, own logistics, AI recommendations.
4. Structure: `src/pages/` routes; `src/components/` UI; `src/lib/` business logic; `src/types/` domain; `src/context/` state. SPA with react-router-dom.

## Code style
5. TypeScript strict: no `any`; prefer `interface` for objects and `type` for unions.
6. Naming: components/types — PascalCase; functions/hooks — camelCase.
7. Styles — Tailwind only; no inline `style={{}}`.
8. Imports via `@/` alias; pure business logic in `lib/`.

## Constraints
9. FORBIDDEN: TypeScript `any`.
10. FORBIDDEN: Moment.js, styled-components without request, deprecated patterns.
11. FORBIDDEN: delivery date earlier than today + 2 calendar days.
12. FORBIDDEN: hardcoding secrets or real payment keys.

## Output format
13. Brief plan, then code with paths, then how to verify.
14. Do not invent nonexistent APIs; state assumptions explicitly.
